WEBVTT

1
00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:39.279
(JOSH SNORING)

2
00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.944
(CREAKING)

3
00:06:13.672 --> 00:06:14.941
Mom?

4
00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.410
Hey. sweetie.

5
00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:20.413
What are you doing up?
Come here.

6
00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:22.014
I don't like my room.

7
00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.150
No?

8
00:06:25.717 --> 00:06:28.653
That's okay.
You know. you're still
getting used to it.

9
00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.257
I can't sleep either.

10
00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:33.459
What are you
looking at?

11
00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.995
Some old photos.
You want to see?

12
00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.368
Do you know
who that is?

13
00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:44.470
No.

14
00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:46.272
It's me.

15
00:06:46.338 --> 00:06:47.673
It doesn't
look like you.

16
00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.742
(LAUGHS)

17
00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:53.246
I know.
But that's me.
That's your mom.

18
00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:56.282
I was a kid once. too.
believe it or not.

19
00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.317
You're old now.

20
00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:01.420
How old do you
think I am?

21
00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:01.487
Really old.

22
00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:02.789
Oh.

23
00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.458
Have a guess.

24
00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:09.462
Probably at least. uh. 21.

25
00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.533
(SIGHS) I wish
you were right.

26
00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.002
Show me a picture
of when Dad
was a little kid.

27
00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:18.137
You know.
I wish I could.

28
00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:19.805
But I don't think
we have any.

29
00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:22.307
He's really hopeless
at keeping photos.

30
00:07:22.374 --> 00:07:25.244
Show me
a picture of when
I was a little kid.

31
00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:28.714
You are a little kid.
You're wonderful.

32
00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.216
(CALI CRYING)

33
00:07:33.518 --> 00:07:35.921
You certainly
didn't cry as much
as your little sister.

34
00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:39.158
But she's up.
so let's go.
Get some breakfast.

35
00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:40.259
Billing department.

36
00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:41.360
Let me play.

37
00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:41.427
No.

38
00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:42.795
I want to play!

39
00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:42.862
I'm eating breakfast!

40
00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:44.597
Billing department. Careful.

41
00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:45.831
FOSTER: I need
a bowl. Mom.

42
00:07:45.897 --> 00:07:48.467
I don't want to play soon.
I want to play now.

43
00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:50.402
DALTON: No. no. no. no.

44
00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:51.771
Here. here.

45
00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:54.540
It's too small.

46
00:07:54.606 --> 00:07:55.875
Well.
just make it work.

47
00:07:58.009 --> 00:08:02.114
Speak to an agent.
Speak to an agent.

48
00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:03.416
(CALI CRYING)

49
00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:16.395
Oh. man. what?

50
00:08:16.461 --> 00:08:18.897
Every time I think
I've pulled you out.

51
00:08:18.964 --> 00:08:21.300
(GRUNTS) you grow back in.

52
00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.370
God.

53
00:08:24.436 --> 00:08:25.504
Good morning. guys.

54
00:08:25.571 --> 00:08:26.905
Speak to an agent!

55
00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:28.074
I'm an agent.

56
00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.575
Yeah. hello.
I would really like

57
00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:30.909
to keep the old number
if that's possible.

58
00:08:30.976 --> 00:08:32.010
Dude. don't eat
on the floor. Foster.

59
00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:33.545
But I'm pouring my cereal.

60
00:08:33.611 --> 00:08:35.780
Can I have it
by the end of the day.
please. because I...

61
00:08:35.847 --> 00:08:38.784
Yes. Okay. Thank you.

62
00:08:40.352 --> 00:08:42.621
Foster.
can you please
get up off the floor?

63
00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:43.823
Cap's loose.

64
00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.830
What is this?
Is that wax?

65
00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:54.467
We have no actual fruit?
We have wax fruit?

66
00:09:04.509 --> 00:09:06.045
God damn it.

67
00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.715
And. honey.
if you wanna
look at my books.

68
00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:11.383
please don't leave them
all over the floor.

69
00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:13.052
I didn't
touch your books.

70
00:09:13.118 --> 00:09:13.118
Bye.

71
00:09:13.118 --> 00:09:14.987
See you. Dad.

72
00:09:15.054 --> 00:09:16.522
See you. buddy.

73
00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:17.989
You're not
gonna take the
boys to school?

74
00:09:18.056 --> 00:09:20.058
I can't today. Bye.

75
00:09:20.125 --> 00:09:21.259
Are you gonna
pick them up?

76
00:09:21.326 --> 00:09:22.627
I can't.
I got a PTA meeting.

77
00:09:22.694 --> 00:09:22.694
I totally forgot.

78
00:09:22.694 --> 00:09:24.296
Why didn't you tell me?

79
00:09:24.362 --> 00:09:27.332
I'm sorry.
Oh. no. no. no.
don't cry. Don't cry.

80
00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:28.568
I'll see you guys. Bye.

81
00:09:31.269 --> 00:09:32.838
(RENAI PLAYING PIANO)

82
00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:39.045
 RENAI:
 <i> ♪ Yeah. I'm looking west</i>

83
00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:43.349
<i> ♪ Always been looking that way</i>

84
00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:48.721
 <i> ♪ I'm gonna get</i>
 <i> it all happening</i>

85
00:09:48.788 --> 00:09:51.891
<i> ♪ Just can't do it today</i>

86
00:09:58.197 --> 00:10:02.034
<i> ♪ Yeah. I'm looking west</i>

87
00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:05.404
<i> ♪ Always been looking that way</i>

88
00:10:06.338 --> 00:10:10.309
<i> ♪ I'm gonna be somebody</i>

89
00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:14.013
<i> ♪ I just can't be her today ♪</i>

90
00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.882
(CALI CRYING
OVER BABY MONITOR)

91
00:10:26.926 --> 00:10:28.294
(CRYING)

92
00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:32.297
It's okay.

93
00:10:32.364 --> 00:10:33.766
(CREAKING NOISE)

94
00:11:30.255 --> 00:11:31.957
(LADDER RUNG BREAKS)

95
00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:39.632
(SIGHS)

96
00:12:04.656 --> 00:12:05.691
JOSH: Hello?

97
00:12:05.758 --> 00:12:07.525
Daddy!

98
00:12:07.592 --> 00:12:10.396
Hey. buddy. slow down...

99
00:12:10.462 --> 00:12:10.462
Whoa! This is awesome!

100
00:12:10.462 --> 00:12:12.898
Share it with your brother.

101
00:12:12.965 --> 00:12:12.965
Okay.

102
00:12:12.965 --> 00:12:14.233
Share with your brother.

103
00:12:14.299 --> 00:12:15.401
Come watch TV with me.

104
00:12:15.468 --> 00:12:17.603
All right.
Look at this. babe.
Nice job!

105
00:12:17.669 --> 00:12:19.305
Yes. it's getting there.

106
00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:20.939
Getting there?

107
00:12:21.006 --> 00:12:21.006
It looks awesome.

108
00:12:21.006 --> 00:12:22.575
Thanks.

109
00:12:23.575 --> 00:12:23.575
Hey.

110
00:12:23.575 --> 00:12:24.610
Hi.

111
00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.251
(GRUNTING)

112
00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.225
(DOOR CREAKING)

113
00:12:47.266 --> 00:12:49.401
Have you seen
my box of sheet
music anywhere?

114
00:12:49.468 --> 00:12:52.871
Uh. I don't know. babe.
I know we packed them.

115
00:12:52.938 --> 00:12:54.973
I packed them.
I know. I just...
I can't find them.

116
00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.976
I think the movers
might have put them
in the dining room.

117
00:12:58.043 --> 00:12:59.077
Come here.
baby girl. come here.

118
00:12:59.144 --> 00:13:00.412
It's not in
the dining room.

119
00:13:00.478 --> 00:13:03.549
I've unpacked
every single box.
and it's just vanished.

120
00:13:03.616 --> 00:13:05.017
I can't find it.

121
00:13:06.185 --> 00:13:09.054
We'll find them.
We'll find them.

122
00:13:49.228 --> 00:13:50.362
(GRUNTS)

123
00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.298
(WOOD CREAKING)

124
00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:10.382
(COOING)

125
00:14:30.068 --> 00:14:31.503
(CREAKING)

126
00:14:41.746 --> 00:14:43.282
(DALTON SCREAMING)

127
00:14:45.851 --> 00:14:48.354
Dalton. honey?
Where are you?

128
00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:54.026
Stay here. Foster.
stay with your sister.

129
00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:54.960
Dalton?

130
00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.495
JOSH: Dalton!

131
00:14:56.561 --> 00:14:57.696
Dalton!

132
00:14:57.762 --> 00:14:59.398
(SCREAMING CONTINUES)

133
00:14:59.465 --> 00:14:59.465
RENAI: Hey!

134
00:14:59.465 --> 00:15:01.099
JOSH: What?

135
00:15:01.166 --> 00:15:02.768
Hey. hey. Hey.

136
00:15:02.835 --> 00:15:02.835
(STOPS SCREAMING)

137
00:15:02.835 --> 00:15:04.503
What happened?

138
00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:06.672
Did you fall?
Did you fall off the ladder?
Honey. did you fall down?

139
00:15:06.739 --> 00:15:06.739
Yeah.

140
00:15:06.739 --> 00:15:08.373
Are you okay?

141
00:15:08.439 --> 00:15:08.439
What are you doing
climbing the ladder?

142
00:15:08.439 --> 00:15:09.507
Honey...

143
00:15:09.574 --> 00:15:11.143
Sorry. Sorry.

144
00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:12.578
Are you okay?

145
00:15:13.345 --> 00:15:14.413
What hurts? What hurts?

146
00:15:14.479 --> 00:15:16.615
My leg.

147
00:15:16.682 --> 00:15:19.518
All right. Can you move it?
Can you move your leg?
Is that okay?

148
00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:19.585
Yeah.

149
00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:21.486
Okay.

150
00:15:21.553 --> 00:15:23.088
Oh. man.
What happened to your head?

151
00:15:23.155 --> 00:15:23.155
Oh. gosh!

152
00:15:23.155 --> 00:15:24.556
Scraped it.

153
00:15:24.623 --> 00:15:27.492
Okay. (PANTING)

154
00:15:27.559 --> 00:15:30.529
Honey. you cannot
come up here. okay?
Do not explore anymore.

155
00:15:30.595 --> 00:15:33.165
It's very dangerous. okay?
It's off limits now.

156
00:15:33.231 --> 00:15:34.399
I'm sorry. Mom.

157
00:15:34.466 --> 00:15:35.934
Okay. Okay.
It's okay. It's okay.

158
00:15:36.001 --> 00:15:37.169
Can you stand on it?

159
00:15:37.235 --> 00:15:37.235
Be careful.

160
00:15:37.235 --> 00:15:38.503
I think so.

161
00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:40.038
I got you. Come here.

162
00:15:40.105 --> 00:15:43.642
What are you doing?
You scared us. buddy.

163
00:15:43.709 --> 00:15:46.711
You were just doing
a little exploring?

164
00:15:46.778 --> 00:15:47.980
DALTON: Yeah.

165
00:15:56.721 --> 00:15:58.890
RENAI: So. no more
exploring up there. okay?

166
00:15:58.957 --> 00:16:00.559
DALTON: Okay.

167
00:16:00.626 --> 00:16:04.463
Yeah. you may be
a superhero. buddy.
but you're not invincible.

168
00:16:04.529 --> 00:16:06.030
You gotta be careful.
all right?

169
00:16:06.097 --> 00:16:07.099
Okay.

170
00:16:07.666 --> 00:16:08.834
Yeah.

171
00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.038
Good night. sweetie.

172
00:16:16.041 --> 00:16:17.476
So were you
putting boxes
away upstairs?

173
00:16:18.443 --> 00:16:19.511
Don't. Josh.

174
00:16:20.512 --> 00:16:23.348
I just hate feeling
helpless. Sorry.

175
00:16:23.415 --> 00:16:25.083
I'll figure out
a way to lock
the door tomorrow.

176
00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:28.553
Good.
It's dangerous. you know.

177
00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:31.122
Maybe we should
just put him on
a child leash.

178
00:16:31.189 --> 00:16:32.825
I'll stop at
the pet store tomorrow.

179
00:16:37.062 --> 00:16:39.664
I'm sorry I was pissy
when you got home
from work today.

180
00:16:39.731 --> 00:16:41.299
No. didn't notice.

181
00:16:41.366 --> 00:16:45.637
I was trying
to do some work
today and then

182
00:16:45.704 --> 00:16:49.074
Cali woke up
after a half hour. and...

183
00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:51.777
And she wouldn't
go back down.

184
00:16:51.844 --> 00:16:53.679
and I just didn't
get anything done.

185
00:16:57.549 --> 00:17:00.152
I just want things to be
different in this house.

186
00:17:00.219 --> 00:17:01.553
Mmm.

187
00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:02.787
I just had
such a bad day.

188
00:17:02.854 --> 00:17:04.255
I'm scared nothing
is gonna change.

189
00:17:04.321 --> 00:17:06.424
It will.
I promise you.

190
00:17:06.491 --> 00:17:08.260
We've just got
to give it time.

191
00:17:12.263 --> 00:17:15.365
Thanks for letting me
take some time to
work on my music.

192
00:17:15.433 --> 00:17:17.669
Come on.
I want you to do it.

193
00:17:19.304 --> 00:17:20.472
I think I have
a couple of good songs.

194
00:17:20.538 --> 00:17:22.607
I mean.
not all of them.
but I think...

195
00:17:22.674 --> 00:17:26.211
You know.
there's a few that
I can do something with.

196
00:17:27.377 --> 00:17:28.545
I love all your songs.

197
00:17:28.613 --> 00:17:28.613
Shut up. You do not!

198
00:17:28.613 --> 00:17:31.050
I do. Stop it.

199
00:17:33.819 --> 00:17:35.353
Which one's
your favorite?

200
00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:35.420
Ooh.

201
00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:36.955
(LAUGHS)

202
00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.958
You should write
a song about me.

203
00:17:40.024 --> 00:17:41.627
They're all about you.

204
00:17:41.693 --> 00:17:43.796
Like how cool I am.

205
00:17:43.862 --> 00:17:45.697
Like.
"He's the coolest guy..."

206
00:17:45.764 --> 00:17:47.432
No. no. no. no. no.

207
00:17:47.498 --> 00:17:50.134
No. no. no.
Shh. Quiet.

208
00:17:50.201 --> 00:17:52.237
"Big muscles!"

209
00:17:52.303 --> 00:17:53.705
"Really. really pretty!"

210
00:17:53.771 --> 00:17:55.707
Shh. you'll
wake up the baby.

211
00:17:55.773 --> 00:17:55.773
(MUMBLES)

212
00:17:55.773 --> 00:17:57.042
Shh.

213
00:18:45.957 --> 00:18:47.859
Foster. can you finish
your eggs. please?

214
00:18:47.926 --> 00:18:49.061
(CRYING)

215
00:18:49.127 --> 00:18:50.662
Hey. Cali.

216
00:18:52.096 --> 00:18:54.032
Can you go
wake up Dalton. Josh?

217
00:18:54.099 --> 00:18:55.267
Yeah.

218
00:18:59.504 --> 00:19:01.740
Hey.
Mr. Sleepy-pants. Get up.

219
00:19:03.375 --> 00:19:05.443
(CHUCKLES)

220
00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:09.013
Hey. Sleepy-pants.
You'd better get
out of that bed

221
00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:11.683
or your mother's
gonna kill us both.

222
00:19:15.253 --> 00:19:17.122
Dalton. come on. buddy.
You gotta get
ready for school.

223
00:19:19.825 --> 00:19:21.927
Hey. Hey.

224
00:19:24.663 --> 00:19:25.931
Dalton.

225
00:19:28.967 --> 00:19:30.169
Dalton?

226
00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:36.741
Dalton. Dalton.
Dalton. Dalton!

227
00:19:36.808 --> 00:19:40.645
There is no brain damage
that we've detected.

228
00:19:40.712 --> 00:19:43.014
Technically. yes.
he's in a coma.

229
00:19:43.081 --> 00:19:46.218
He doesn't react to stimuli.
He has no sleep-wake cycle.

230
00:19:46.284 --> 00:19:51.289
But there's no brain
trauma or infection.
His scans are all normal.

231
00:19:51.356 --> 00:19:54.626
To be honest.
I've never seen
anything like it.

232
00:19:54.693 --> 00:19:58.663
But he can't
just not wake up.
I mean...

233
00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:01.166
There's got
to be something.

234
00:20:01.899 --> 00:20:03.402
I'm sorry.

235
00:20:05.737 --> 00:20:08.039
Okay. so...
So what do we do?

236
00:20:08.106 --> 00:20:09.508
Does he stay here?
Do we...

237
00:20:09.575 --> 00:20:11.042
We'll conduct
some further testing.

238
00:20:11.109 --> 00:20:12.443
It's only been
a couple of days.

239
00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:12.510
It could take
a little longer for...

240
00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:15.413
(PAGER BEEPING)

241
00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:18.516
Excuse me a minute.
I have to step out.
I'll be back in just a moment.

242
00:20:18.583 --> 00:20:21.220
Dr. Sercarz.
how long will
the tests take?

243
00:20:24.522 --> 00:20:26.158
(ECG BEEPING)

244
00:20:37.369 --> 00:20:38.870
NURSE: Okay. so what
I've done here is

245
00:20:38.937 --> 00:20:41.239
I've inserted
a nasogastric feeding tube.

246
00:20:41.306 --> 00:20:44.676
To get the length
of the tube that
I'm gonna need.

247
00:20:44.743 --> 00:20:48.045
I measure from
the tip of the
nose to the earlobe

248
00:20:48.112 --> 00:20:51.516
and down to the
xiphoid process.
which is here.

249
00:20:51.582 --> 00:20:54.986
Then I usually
mark that off
with some tape.

250
00:20:55.052 --> 00:20:57.855
And then you
need to lubricate
the end of the tube

251
00:20:57.922 --> 00:21:00.726
that I'm
going to insert
about four inches.

252
00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:05.029
And then I just
slide it in like that.

253
00:21:05.096 --> 00:21:06.631
I have to make sure
the end of the tube

254
00:21:06.698 --> 00:21:08.800
is curved
and that his head
is a little bent.

255
00:21:08.866 --> 00:21:12.704
a little bent back.

256
00:21:12.771 --> 00:21:15.873
And then we usually
hold it in place with
some surgical tape.

257
00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:18.476
And that's it.

258
00:21:18.543 --> 00:21:19.811
(VOICE ECHOING)
If there's any problems

259
00:21:19.878 --> 00:21:22.514
or any bleeding.
just call me. okay?

260
00:21:23.348 --> 00:21:24.983
(INDISTINCT)

261
00:21:37.929 --> 00:21:39.898
(PLAYING)

262
00:21:43.234 --> 00:21:45.137
(PLAYS WRONG NOTE)

263
00:21:51.209 --> 00:21:52.778
(STATIC ON BABY MONITOR)

264
00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.723
(WHIRLING NOISES)

265
00:22:18.236 --> 00:22:22.140
MALE VOICE:<i>
 There's nothing you can do.
 Nothing you can do.</i>

266
00:22:28.346 --> 00:22:30.282
(INDISTINCT WHISPERING
ON BABY MONITOR)

267
00:22:51.702 --> 00:22:53.205
(CHUCKLING)

268
00:22:56.774 --> 00:22:58.076
<i> I want it!</i>

269
00:22:58.143 --> 00:23:01.346
Give me it!
Give me it!
I want it!

270
00:23:01.413 --> 00:23:03.348
I want it...
(ROARS) Now!

271
00:23:03.948 --> 00:23:05.150
(CALI CRYING)

272
00:23:19.263 --> 00:23:22.634
Hey. hey. hey.
It's okay.

273
00:23:23.467 --> 00:23:26.738
It's okay. It's okay.

274
00:23:29.774 --> 00:23:31.943
It's okay. It's okay.

275
00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:04.342
What's this?

276
00:24:04.408 --> 00:24:05.610
An award.

277
00:24:07.612 --> 00:24:11.183
That's today's date.
Did you get this today?

278
00:24:12.784 --> 00:24:15.420
Honey.
why didn't you tell us?

279
00:24:20.525 --> 00:24:23.028
I know it's
hard right now.

280
00:24:23.094 --> 00:24:25.630
but things
are going to
get better. I promise.

281
00:24:28.266 --> 00:24:30.001
I'm gonna show
this to your dad.

282
00:24:30.068 --> 00:24:31.670
It's fantastic.

283
00:24:36.607 --> 00:24:38.443
I'm scared. Mom.

284
00:24:42.614 --> 00:24:43.982
Scared of what?

285
00:24:44.582 --> 00:24:46.117
Dalton.

286
00:24:46.184 --> 00:24:47.986
Can I change rooms?

287
00:24:49.086 --> 00:24:51.589
Why would you want
to change rooms?

288
00:24:51.656 --> 00:24:54.459
I don't like
when he walks
around at night.

289
00:25:01.232 --> 00:25:03.701
(BEEPING)

290
00:25:03.768 --> 00:25:05.237
(RADIO STATIC SOUNDING)

291
00:25:09.674 --> 00:25:11.109
(CREAKING)

292
00:25:57.422 --> 00:25:58.790
(CREAKING)

293
00:26:03.294 --> 00:26:04.729
(THUDDING)

294
00:26:08.299 --> 00:26:10.669
Something really weird
happened to me today.

295
00:26:10.735 --> 00:26:12.771
Huh. What?

296
00:26:12.837 --> 00:26:15.639
I heard
this noise coming
from Cali's room.

297
00:26:15.706 --> 00:26:18.743
It was on
the baby monitor.
It was like voices.

298
00:26:18.810 --> 00:26:20.912
And I ran up here
and I had a look.

299
00:26:20.978 --> 00:26:23.848
but there was
no one in there.

300
00:26:23.914 --> 00:26:26.384
(CHUCKLES)
It was probably
just interference.

301
00:26:26.451 --> 00:26:28.819
Those things are
always picking up
somebody else's signal.

302
00:26:28.886 --> 00:26:30.988
I don't know.
It sounded so clear.

303
00:26:31.055 --> 00:26:32.890
It was like
this whispering.

304
00:26:32.957 --> 00:26:36.494
It was...
It scared the
hell out of me.

305
00:26:36.561 --> 00:26:38.796
I was at the piano.
and I could hear it
on the monitor.

306
00:26:38.863 --> 00:26:40.764
and I turned up
the volume and...

307
00:26:40.831 --> 00:26:42.067
(BANGING ON DOOR)

308
00:26:43.434 --> 00:26:44.869
Who the hell is that?

309
00:26:47.671 --> 00:26:48.706
(BANGING REPEATS)

310
00:26:48.773 --> 00:26:49.975
Hold on.

311
00:26:50.975 --> 00:26:52.077
Stay here.

312
00:27:11.529 --> 00:27:12.864
Who is it?

313
00:27:33.218 --> 00:27:34.386
Jesus.

314
00:27:35.487 --> 00:27:36.688
(SIGHS)

315
00:27:48.032 --> 00:27:49.334
Hello?

316
00:28:04.449 --> 00:28:05.517
(BEEPS)

317
00:28:10.488 --> 00:28:12.390
(CALI WAILING OVER MONITOR)

318
00:28:23.134 --> 00:28:23.134
(CALI CRYING)

319
00:28:23.134 --> 00:28:26.104
Oh. my God!
Josh! Josh! Josh!

320
00:28:26.170 --> 00:28:29.440
Please.
Someone's in Cali's room!
Someone's in Cali's room!

321
00:28:29.507 --> 00:28:31.409
There's someone there!
I saw somebody!

322
00:28:33.311 --> 00:28:35.847
He was standing right there!
He was standing right there!

323
00:28:40.151 --> 00:28:40.151
There's nobody here.

324
00:28:40.151 --> 00:28:42.320
I saw someone!

325
00:28:42.387 --> 00:28:44.522
(ALARM BLARING)

326
00:28:44.588 --> 00:28:47.826
Okay. okay.
take her. get Foster.
go in Dalton's room.

327
00:28:51.329 --> 00:28:52.897
(ALARM CONTINUES BLARING)

328
00:29:03.274 --> 00:29:03.274
Foster!

329
00:29:03.274 --> 00:29:04.442
What's going on?

330
00:29:04.508 --> 00:29:05.877
The alarm's gone off!

331
00:29:17.955 --> 00:29:19.057
(ALARM STOPS)

332
00:29:40.010 --> 00:29:41.846
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

333
00:30:12.443 --> 00:30:12.443
(ALARM STARS BLARING)

334
00:30:12.443 --> 00:30:14.312
God damn it!

335
00:30:24.622 --> 00:30:25.890
(ALARM STOPS)

336
00:30:32.763 --> 00:30:33.864
(SCHOOL BELL RINGING)

337
00:30:33.931 --> 00:30:35.400
Thanks. guys.

338
00:30:38.969 --> 00:30:40.271
I'll see you tomorrow.

339
00:30:50.715 --> 00:30:52.183
(EXHALES)

340
00:30:52.250 --> 00:30:54.685
Hey. honey.
It's me. Um...

341
00:30:54.751 --> 00:30:56.553
They just told me.
I've got to. uh...

342
00:30:56.620 --> 00:30:58.622
I'm gonna have to
stay late tonight to...

343
00:30:58.689 --> 00:31:03.227
I gotta grade some tests.
and it's gonna be
a while so. um...

344
00:31:03.294 --> 00:31:05.296
You don't have
to wait up. okay?

345
00:31:05.362 --> 00:31:07.599
I'll be home
as soon as I can.
I love you.

346
00:31:39.697 --> 00:31:40.999
(CAR HORN HONKS)

347
00:31:45.369 --> 00:31:49.540
Did he respond to
any of the new tests?

348
00:31:49.607 --> 00:31:52.643
No. No. he didn't.

349
00:31:52.710 --> 00:31:54.645
But we have to
give it time.

350
00:31:54.712 --> 00:31:57.081
I've seen coma patients
with a much longer
inactivity time

351
00:31:57.148 --> 00:31:59.350
suddenly start
making noises.

352
00:32:00.484 --> 00:32:02.120
He's not in a coma.

353
00:32:03.754 --> 00:32:05.590
They don't know
what to call it.

354
00:32:08.125 --> 00:32:10.361
They don't know
what to do with him.

355
00:32:11.495 --> 00:32:13.464
so they've
just given up.

356
00:32:14.999 --> 00:32:17.968
I feel like
the universe is just

357
00:32:18.035 --> 00:32:22.306
trying to see
how far I'll bend
before I break.

358
00:32:22.373 --> 00:32:25.310
Well. the universe
picked a fight with
the wrong chick.

359
00:32:28.979 --> 00:32:31.182
That's okay.
I got it.

360
00:32:32.650 --> 00:32:34.052
Thank you.

361
00:32:41.759 --> 00:32:42.894
Okay.

362
00:33:16.927 --> 00:33:18.129
(SIGHS)

363
00:33:22.032 --> 00:33:23.401
(PHONE CHIMES)

364
00:33:28.339 --> 00:33:30.808
 RENAI: (ON VOICEMAIL)
 <i> Josh. where are you?</i>

365
00:33:30.875 --> 00:33:34.012
 <i> I need you to come</i>
 <i> home now. please.</i>

366
00:33:49.760 --> 00:33:51.129
It's 10:30.

367
00:33:52.496 --> 00:33:54.197
Mmm-hmm.

368
00:33:54.264 --> 00:33:57.101
You've been
coming home late
every single night.

369
00:33:58.369 --> 00:33:59.636
In all the years
you've worked at the school.

370
00:33:59.703 --> 00:34:00.872
you've never
had to do that.

371
00:34:00.938 --> 00:34:03.340
Why all of a sudden
are you staying back late?

372
00:34:03.407 --> 00:34:05.076
You know.
I don't like it either.

373
00:34:05.142 --> 00:34:07.712
I was grading tests.
I mean...

374
00:34:07.778 --> 00:34:09.479
What choice do I have?

375
00:34:09.545 --> 00:34:09.545
I've got to pay
Dalton's bills.

376
00:34:09.545 --> 00:34:11.648
Josh.

377
00:34:11.716 --> 00:34:15.153
I'm scared.
I'm so scared and...

378
00:34:16.454 --> 00:34:19.623
I'm scared.
He's my son. too.

379
00:34:19.690 --> 00:34:23.394
You don't understand.
I'm scared for Dalton.

380
00:34:23.460 --> 00:34:24.762
I'm scared
of this house.

381
00:34:30.134 --> 00:34:31.902
There's something
wrong with this place.

382
00:34:31.969 --> 00:34:35.039
I'm not imagining it.
I can feel it.

383
00:34:35.105 --> 00:34:36.440
It's like a sickness.

384
00:34:36.507 --> 00:34:40.078
Ever since we've moved in.
everything's just gone wrong.

385
00:34:44.848 --> 00:34:46.583
You think
our house is haunted?

386
00:34:46.650 --> 00:34:48.886
I don't think it.
I know it.

387
00:34:48.953 --> 00:34:50.787
Things move
around in here
by themselves.

388
00:34:50.853 --> 00:34:55.125
I walk into the kitchen
at night to get a drink.
I can feel eyes on me.

389
00:34:56.594 --> 00:35:00.697
I can't be in there
alone anymore.

390
00:35:00.764 --> 00:35:05.002
I need you.
But you're never here.

391
00:35:05.069 --> 00:35:06.270
Where are you?

392
00:35:06.337 --> 00:35:09.073
I told you.
I was grading tests.

393
00:35:09.807 --> 00:35:11.909
That's not what I mean.

394
00:35:11.976 --> 00:35:14.111
You're not here
with me in this situation.

395
00:35:14.177 --> 00:35:17.180
You're just
avoiding it.

396
00:35:17.247 --> 00:35:20.518
like everything stressful.
whether it's this
or parking tickets.

397
00:35:20.584 --> 00:35:21.885
Oh. God.
Stop saying that. okay?

398
00:35:21.952 --> 00:35:24.222
I don't avoid
stressful situations.

399
00:35:24.288 --> 00:35:27.358
I'm just dealing with it
in my own fucking way.

400
00:35:31.895 --> 00:35:33.064
(SIGHS)

401
00:35:37.501 --> 00:35:39.470
Fine. Deal with this!

402
00:35:43.140 --> 00:35:44.208
(DOOR CLOSES)

403
00:36:21.112 --> 00:36:22.580
(CREAKING)

404
00:36:25.649 --> 00:36:26.951
(SCREAMS)

405
00:36:28.052 --> 00:36:29.353
(PANTING)

406
00:36:50.675 --> 00:36:51.876
Jesus.

407
00:36:52.743 --> 00:36:54.011
Oh. God.

408
00:37:11.629 --> 00:37:13.297
(FLOOR THUDDING)

409
00:37:14.431 --> 00:37:15.733
Josh?

410
00:37:20.938 --> 00:37:22.173
Josh.

411
00:37:29.280 --> 00:37:29.280
(SCREAMING)

412
00:37:29.280 --> 00:37:31.015
(SCREECHING)

413
00:37:32.816 --> 00:37:34.151
(RENAI SCREAMING)

414
00:37:34.218 --> 00:37:35.653
(CALI CRYING)

415
00:37:37.688 --> 00:37:38.956
Renai?

416
00:37:43.093 --> 00:37:43.093
Renai!

417
00:37:43.093 --> 00:37:44.662
(SCREAMING)

418
00:37:45.829 --> 00:37:47.364
What. what. what?
What is it?

419
00:37:47.431 --> 00:37:48.565
There's someone here.

420
00:37:48.632 --> 00:37:50.268
There's someone
in the room!

421
00:37:51.402 --> 00:37:53.871
He was right there.
I swear!

422
00:37:58.776 --> 00:38:02.012
Don't you dare
not believe me.

423
00:38:02.079 --> 00:38:04.982
(CRYING) Please.
Please. believe me.

424
00:38:05.049 --> 00:38:07.551
I swear
he was right there.

425
00:38:07.617 --> 00:38:09.420
I do. I do.
I do believe you.

426
00:38:09.487 --> 00:38:11.688
I just don't know
what you want me to do.

427
00:38:11.755 --> 00:38:14.991
I want to leave. Please.
I want to leave this house.

428
00:38:15.058 --> 00:38:17.728
I can't spend
another night here. Please!

429
00:38:17.795 --> 00:38:17.795
Please. help me!

430
00:38:17.795 --> 00:38:19.930
Okay. okay. okay.

431
00:38:22.098 --> 00:38:23.734
We're going.

432
00:38:45.723 --> 00:38:48.225
Lorraine. please.
you shouldn't be doing
any of this. Just sit down.

433
00:38:48.292 --> 00:38:50.394
I'm perfectly capable
of putting a few things away.

434
00:38:50.461 --> 00:38:51.862
I did it for Josh
his whole life.

435
00:38:51.929 --> 00:38:54.432
I know.
but I feel terrible.

436
00:38:56.267 --> 00:39:00.237
I think it's you who
should be sitting down
by the looks of it.

437
00:39:04.341 --> 00:39:07.945
I can't believe
you got Josh to
hold still for a photo.

438
00:39:08.012 --> 00:39:12.350
What I can't believe is
that we are doing this
all over again.

439
00:39:13.383 --> 00:39:14.752
Ridiculous.

440
00:39:19.489 --> 00:39:21.559
You must think
I'm crazy.

441
00:39:22.626 --> 00:39:24.561
Nobody.

442
00:39:24.628 --> 00:39:28.632
not me or anybody.
knows what you're
going through right now.

443
00:39:28.699 --> 00:39:32.002
Whatever you have to do
to get through it. do it.

444
00:39:33.370 --> 00:39:35.873
And you don't have to
apologize for anything.

445
00:39:39.710 --> 00:39:41.178
Thanks.

446
00:39:48.752 --> 00:39:50.388
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

447
00:40:41.472 --> 00:40:43.407
(RECORD SCRATCHING)

448
00:40:44.207 --> 00:40:46.876
(RADIO STATIC SOUNDING)

449
00:40:46.943 --> 00:40:48.178
 <i> (TIPTOE THROUGH THE TULIPS</i>
 PLAYING)

450
00:40:48.245 --> 00:40:51.014
<i> ♪ Tiptoe through the window</i>

451
00:40:51.081 --> 00:40:54.618
 <i> ♪ By the window.</i>
 <i> that is where I'll be</i>

452
00:40:54.685 --> 00:41:00.257
 <i> ♪ Come tiptoe</i>
 <i> through the tulips with me</i>

453
00:41:03.460 --> 00:41:06.497
<i> ♪ Tiptoe from the garden</i>

454
00:41:06.564 --> 00:41:10.033
 <i> ♪ By the garden</i>
 <i> of the willow tree</i>

455
00:41:10.100 --> 00:41:15.039
 <i> ♪ And tiptoe</i>
 <i> through the tulips with me ♪</i>

456
00:41:26.149 --> 00:41:27.485
(SONG STOPS)

457
00:41:36.694 --> 00:41:38.395
(DOOR SQUEAKING)

458
00:41:40.197 --> 00:41:41.432
(CHILD LAUGHING)

459
00:41:44.768 --> 00:41:46.103
(CHUCKLING)

460
00:42:51.735 --> 00:42:53.904
(DALTON'S
HEART MONITOR BEEPING)

461
00:42:53.971 --> 00:42:55.539
(CHILD LAUGHING)

462
00:42:58.275 --> 00:42:59.577
Dalton?

463
00:43:36.814 --> 00:43:37.848
(LAUGHING PLAYFULLY)

464
00:43:43.353 --> 00:43:44.622
(CRYING)

465
00:43:48.358 --> 00:43:52.229
Your faith can help.
Trust it. you know.

466
00:43:52.796 --> 00:43:54.031
Hello.

467
00:43:54.098 --> 00:43:55.332
Josh.

468
00:43:57.233 --> 00:43:58.635
This is the first line
of a joke. right?

469
00:43:58.702 --> 00:44:01.939
A guy comes home
to find his wife
with a priest.

470
00:44:02.005 --> 00:44:03.740
Uh. this is
Liam Martin.

471
00:44:03.807 --> 00:44:03.807
Nice to meet you.

472
00:44:03.807 --> 00:44:06.776
He's actually a very
old friend of mine.

473
00:44:06.843 --> 00:44:08.979
This is my husband. Josh.

474
00:44:09.045 --> 00:44:10.547
What's going on here?

475
00:44:10.614 --> 00:44:10.614
I should be going.

476
00:44:10.614 --> 00:44:11.648
Thank you.

477
00:44:11.715 --> 00:44:12.883
Thank you so much.

478
00:44:12.949 --> 00:44:14.451
Thank you
so much for the tea.

479
00:44:17.987 --> 00:44:21.125
This thing from
the other house

480
00:44:22.525 --> 00:44:24.294
has followed us here.

481
00:44:24.360 --> 00:44:28.398
I saw something today.

482
00:44:28.465 --> 00:44:29.933
I thought it was
a little boy.

483
00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:32.135
I followed it
into Dalton's room.

484
00:44:32.202 --> 00:44:36.339
But it wasn't a child.
It was something else.

485
00:44:36.406 --> 00:44:41.778
So what? You just
brought a priest in
to get rid of it?

486
00:44:41.845 --> 00:44:43.846
I didn't know
what else to do. Josh.

487
00:44:43.913 --> 00:44:46.115
Come on. Renai.

488
00:44:46.182 --> 00:44:48.252
When's the last time
you went to church?

489
00:44:51.621 --> 00:44:54.124
What's happening
to Renai is real.

490
00:44:54.992 --> 00:44:56.493
I've seen it for myself.

491
00:44:59.295 --> 00:45:01.731
I came today
because last night

492
00:45:01.798 --> 00:45:03.567
I had a dream
about this place.

493
00:45:05.134 --> 00:45:08.439
I was in this house.
but it was late at night.

494
00:45:11.741 --> 00:45:14.278
<i> I was afraid.</i>

495
00:45:19.983 --> 00:45:23.253
 <i> I went into your bedroom.</i>
 <i> but you were both asleep.</i>

496
00:45:26.523 --> 00:45:30.060
I knew
I was asleep
in the dream.

497
00:45:30.127 --> 00:45:33.397
but I could feel
that someone was awake

498
00:45:34.130 --> 00:45:35.699
in the house.

499
00:45:38.134 --> 00:45:39.770
I went
into Dalton's room.

500
00:45:53.116 --> 00:45:54.718
There was something
in there with him.

501
00:45:59.522 --> 00:46:01.658
It was
standing there
in the corner.

502
00:46:06.196 --> 00:46:09.199
I asked it.
"Who are you?"

503
00:46:09.265 --> 00:46:12.569
And it said
it was a visitor.

504
00:46:14.204 --> 00:46:15.873
I said.
"What do you want?"

505
00:46:16.873 --> 00:46:18.609
(CREAKING)

506
00:46:22.479 --> 00:46:23.814
It said. "Dalton."

507
00:46:29.586 --> 00:46:31.722
I can still
hear that voice.

508
00:46:33.690 --> 00:46:34.758
(CREAKING)

509
00:46:36.025 --> 00:46:37.093
(SCREAMS)

510
00:46:37.160 --> 00:46:38.428
What? What?

511
00:46:38.928 --> 00:46:39.996
It's here!

512
00:46:40.063 --> 00:46:41.097
What?

513
00:46:41.164 --> 00:46:42.533
(THUDDING)

514
00:46:58.114 --> 00:46:59.416
(BANGS)

515
00:47:08.525 --> 00:47:09.993
Jesus!

516
00:47:10.059 --> 00:47:11.195
Oh. my God!

517
00:47:16.365 --> 00:47:18.468
JOSH: Okay. He's okay.

518
00:47:18.535 --> 00:47:21.238
Please! Please.
help him! Please!

519
00:47:25.842 --> 00:47:27.144
I know someone
who can help

520
00:47:29.445 --> 00:47:31.248
if you're
willing to ask.

521
00:47:37.954 --> 00:47:40.757
I'm Specs.
This is Tucker.

522
00:47:40.824 --> 00:47:40.824
I'm Renai. Hi.

523
00:47:40.824 --> 00:47:42.092
Hi.

524
00:47:42.159 --> 00:47:42.159
You must be Josh.

525
00:47:42.159 --> 00:47:44.894
Yeah. Hi.

526
00:47:44.961 --> 00:47:48.465
That wasn't psychic.
Elise already told me
your name so...

527
00:47:48.532 --> 00:47:50.033
Where is Elise?

528
00:47:50.100 --> 00:47:53.169
She sent us
ahead to do some
preliminary tests.

529
00:47:53.236 --> 00:47:55.472
Helps weed out
the nut jobs.

530
00:47:57.574 --> 00:47:58.609
Hmm.

531
00:48:02.445 --> 00:48:03.546
(BLOWS)

532
00:48:03.613 --> 00:48:04.814
RENAI: What is that?

533
00:48:04.881 --> 00:48:06.316
TUCKER: It's
a Trifield meter.

534
00:48:06.383 --> 00:48:08.017
Measures DC fields

535
00:48:08.084 --> 00:48:12.522
and the natural
electromagnetic environment.

536
00:48:12.589 --> 00:48:15.658
Yeah. sometimes
old wiring can leak
into the atmosphere.

537
00:48:15.725 --> 00:48:18.695
It causes hallucinations.
changes in energy.

538
00:48:18.761 --> 00:48:21.731
It's a little more
important than that.
but whatever.

539
00:48:21.798 --> 00:48:24.034
The tech stuff's
not really relevant
to you guys anyway.

540
00:48:24.101 --> 00:48:25.402
It's all very
relevant. actually.

541
00:48:27.303 --> 00:48:28.772
(MACHINE PULSING)

542
00:48:34.244 --> 00:48:35.779
(STATIC)

543
00:48:35.846 --> 00:48:36.880
(EXHALES)

544
00:48:38.281 --> 00:48:38.281
(SPECS GASPS)

545
00:48:38.281 --> 00:48:40.117
What?

546
00:48:41.384 --> 00:48:43.186
Starfleet Series One.

547
00:48:45.421 --> 00:48:47.357
It's hard to find.

548
00:48:47.424 --> 00:48:49.726
Should have
kept it in its box.

549
00:48:52.895 --> 00:48:55.932
This device measures
changes in UV light.

550
00:48:55.999 --> 00:48:58.135
I make
all this equipment
myself. you know.

551
00:48:58.835 --> 00:49:00.003
RENAI: It's impressive.

552
00:49:00.536 --> 00:49:01.838
Thanks.

553
00:49:03.439 --> 00:49:06.542
It's not that hard
if you know
what you're doing.

554
00:49:06.609 --> 00:49:09.713
Yeah.
that one's basically
a modified toy.

555
00:49:13.316 --> 00:49:16.053
I'm gonna need
some time alone
to concentrate.

556
00:49:25.561 --> 00:49:27.130
(MACHINE PULSING)

557
00:49:40.476 --> 00:49:41.945
(STATIC)

558
00:49:45.849 --> 00:49:47.584
(BEEPING)

559
00:50:18.515 --> 00:50:20.317
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

560
00:50:26.956 --> 00:50:29.926
This field is...
Look. the body is
made up of energy.

561
00:50:29.993 --> 00:50:31.160
Where does
that energy go
when we die?

562
00:50:31.227 --> 00:50:33.196
We can call Elise.

563
00:50:34.664 --> 00:50:35.698
Now.

564
00:50:35.765 --> 00:50:36.967
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

565
00:50:39.101 --> 00:50:40.670
(LAUGHING)

566
00:50:40.737 --> 00:50:43.339
I wasn't sure
the doorbell was
working. I'm sorry.

567
00:50:43.406 --> 00:50:43.406
That's fine.
Come on in.

568
00:50:43.406 --> 00:50:44.807
Thank you.

569
00:50:44.874 --> 00:50:46.642
Mrs. Rainier?

570
00:50:46.709 --> 00:50:49.278
No. Mrs. Rainier
is my mother.
Just call me Elise.

571
00:50:49.345 --> 00:50:50.413
I'm Josh.

572
00:50:50.480 --> 00:50:52.015
I knew that.

573
00:50:52.082 --> 00:50:53.817
You've grown since
I last saw you.

574
00:50:54.784 --> 00:50:54.784
Since you last saw me?

575
00:50:54.784 --> 00:50:56.419
Mmm-hmm.

576
00:50:56.486 --> 00:50:59.589
Your mother and I
have been friends
a long time.

577
00:50:59.922 --> 00:51:01.191
Oh.

578
00:51:01.257 --> 00:51:02.525
ELISE: Well. hello.

579
00:51:02.592 --> 00:51:03.593
This is my wife. Renai.

580
00:51:03.659 --> 00:51:04.761
How do you do?

581
00:51:04.828 --> 00:51:05.862
Hi. thank you
for coming.

582
00:51:05.928 --> 00:51:07.030
Thank you
for having me.

583
00:51:07.096 --> 00:51:08.397
Can we get you
anything. Elise?

584
00:51:08.464 --> 00:51:11.000
Oh. no. I'm fine.
thank you so much.

585
00:51:11.067 --> 00:51:14.504
We took Trifield
and EMF readings
of the whole house.

586
00:51:14.571 --> 00:51:17.540
all the wiring.
alarm clocks.
radios. toasters.

587
00:51:17.607 --> 00:51:19.943
TV. record player.
fuse box.

588
00:51:20.009 --> 00:51:22.445
nothing went
off the charts
except for the...

589
00:51:22.511 --> 00:51:23.613
And the previous home?

590
00:51:23.679 --> 00:51:26.182
Um. Tucker hadn't
monitored that yet.

591
00:51:26.249 --> 00:51:27.350
You know what?
Don't even sweat it.

592
00:51:27.417 --> 00:51:28.618
I'll make
myself available.

593
00:51:28.685 --> 00:51:29.786
I'll get on that
this afternoon.

594
00:51:29.853 --> 00:51:32.255
Yeah. but I'll have
to come. too.

595
00:51:32.322 --> 00:51:34.091
because who's going
to operate the equipment?

596
00:51:34.157 --> 00:51:36.559
Well. strictly.
I could do it without...

597
00:51:36.626 --> 00:51:36.626
Yeah. but I need
to oversee...

598
00:51:36.626 --> 00:51:38.561
Yeah. but it's not...

599
00:51:38.628 --> 00:51:40.563
That's fine. gentlemen.

600
00:51:40.630 --> 00:51:43.633
I don't think
bad wiring is
the problem here.

601
00:51:45.435 --> 00:51:48.171
Um. may I walk
through the house?

602
00:51:48.238 --> 00:51:48.238
RENAI: Sure. of course.

603
00:51:48.238 --> 00:51:50.640
Thank you.

604
00:51:50.706 --> 00:51:52.442
Your other children
are with Lorraine. right?

605
00:51:52.509 --> 00:51:55.111
Yeah. they are.

606
00:51:55.178 --> 00:51:56.946
Steven.
do you have
your sketchbook?

607
00:51:57.013 --> 00:51:58.514
Yes. Yes. I do.

608
00:51:58.581 --> 00:52:00.750
Good. 'Cause
we're gonna need it.

609
00:52:00.817 --> 00:52:02.585
What do you
need that for?

610
00:52:02.652 --> 00:52:05.088
Um. she tells me
what she sees.
and I draw it.

611
00:52:05.154 --> 00:52:07.324
It's the most
important part
of her process.

612
00:52:07.390 --> 00:52:07.390
That's debatable.

613
00:52:07.390 --> 00:52:09.359
It's not debatable.

614
00:52:09.426 --> 00:52:11.161
It is.
but whatever.

615
00:52:15.765 --> 00:52:17.367
Leave the light off.

616
00:52:30.947 --> 00:52:32.449
Hey. Dalton.

617
00:52:34.517 --> 00:52:36.853
You are a very
handsome boy.

618
00:52:38.121 --> 00:52:41.158
Your mom
and dad are here.
so don't you worry.

619
00:52:41.991 --> 00:52:43.426
(CREAKING)

620
00:52:55.839 --> 00:52:57.340
(CREAKING CONTINUES)

621
00:52:57.406 --> 00:52:58.942
What? What?

622
00:53:02.479 --> 00:53:03.713
ELISE: The face...

623
00:53:04.313 --> 00:53:05.515
SPECS: What?

624
00:53:06.149 --> 00:53:08.718
Blood red face.

625
00:53:08.784 --> 00:53:12.488
Black...
Black arms.
Black legs.

626
00:53:12.555 --> 00:53:12.555
Black body.

627
00:53:12.555 --> 00:53:14.324
(SCRIBBLING)

628
00:53:14.391 --> 00:53:16.126
(WHISPERING INDISTINCTLY)

629
00:53:21.064 --> 00:53:22.298
Slow down.

630
00:53:22.365 --> 00:53:22.365
His feet are black.
His legs are black.

631
00:53:22.365 --> 00:53:24.634
Slow down.

632
00:53:26.770 --> 00:53:27.971
What is it?

633
00:53:28.672 --> 00:53:30.440
Oh. my God.

634
00:53:30.506 --> 00:53:31.541
(CONTINUES WHISPERING)

635
00:53:34.310 --> 00:53:37.547
And pitch black eyes.
They're like two dark holes.

636
00:53:41.884 --> 00:53:44.020
He has hooves
for feet.

637
00:53:44.921 --> 00:53:46.122
What?

638
00:53:46.189 --> 00:53:47.824
And long
spidery fingernails.

639
00:53:47.890 --> 00:53:48.959
Elise. what's...

640
00:53:50.026 --> 00:53:51.261
Hey. what is that?

641
00:54:09.712 --> 00:54:12.615
I'm not sure
if you're ready
to hear this yet.

642
00:54:12.681 --> 00:54:16.720
but unfortunately.
I can't waste any time
easing you into it.

643
00:54:18.321 --> 00:54:20.556
I want you to know.
this is what I believe.

644
00:54:20.623 --> 00:54:24.694
and it may contradict
a previous medical
diagnosis. but...

645
00:54:24.761 --> 00:54:27.229
You called me here.
and I'm taking that

646
00:54:27.296 --> 00:54:29.833
as an acceptance
of my readings. Yes?

647
00:54:32.769 --> 00:54:34.271
Yes. go on.

648
00:54:38.707 --> 00:54:40.509
Your son
isn't in a coma.

649
00:54:40.576 --> 00:54:43.512
Falling off a ladder
had nothing to do
with this.

650
00:54:43.579 --> 00:54:45.482
His physical body's here.

651
00:54:46.649 --> 00:54:48.717
But his
spiritual body is not.

652
00:54:48.784 --> 00:54:51.020
And the reason
these disturbances.

653
00:54:51.087 --> 00:54:53.789
they followed you
to a new home.

654
00:54:53.856 --> 00:54:57.260
is because
it's not the house
that's haunted.

655
00:54:59.796 --> 00:55:01.298
It's your son.

656
00:55:06.269 --> 00:55:08.038
I don't understand.

657
00:55:09.506 --> 00:55:10.673
(SIGHS)

658
00:55:10.740 --> 00:55:12.575
Have you ever heard
of astral projection?

659
00:55:14.076 --> 00:55:17.614
Yes. It's out of body
experience or something?

660
00:55:18.681 --> 00:55:20.517
I like to
call them travelers.

661
00:55:22.052 --> 00:55:24.187
You see.
these are people
with the ability

662
00:55:24.254 --> 00:55:26.589
to leave their
physical body

663
00:55:26.656 --> 00:55:30.426
and to travel
to different places
in astral form.

664
00:55:30.493 --> 00:55:32.895
Now. Dalton.

665
00:55:32.962 --> 00:55:36.533
he is a very accomplished
astral projector.

666
00:55:38.034 --> 00:55:41.938
He's been
doing it in his sleep
for a long time.

667
00:55:42.005 --> 00:55:45.074
He has been since
he was very young.

668
00:55:45.141 --> 00:55:48.678
And he's unafraid
because he thinks
they're dreams.

669
00:55:48.745 --> 00:55:50.879
And it's that
very lack of fear

670
00:55:50.946 --> 00:55:53.516
that has led him
to travel too far.

671
00:55:54.250 --> 00:55:56.419
And to become lost.

672
00:55:57.053 --> 00:55:58.421
Lost?

673
00:56:00.990 --> 00:56:03.459
Lost where?

674
00:56:03.525 --> 00:56:06.129
In a place that
I call the Further.

675
00:56:06.196 --> 00:56:08.298
What?
What does that mean?

676
00:56:09.566 --> 00:56:12.768
The Further is a world
far beyond our own.

677
00:56:12.835 --> 00:56:14.837
yet it's all around us.

678
00:56:14.904 --> 00:56:17.507
a place
without time
as we know it.

679
00:56:17.573 --> 00:56:22.211
It's a dark realm
filled with the tortured
souls of the dead.

680
00:56:22.278 --> 00:56:24.280
a place not
meant for the living.

681
00:56:27.550 --> 00:56:30.486
That's where Dalton is.

682
00:56:30.553 --> 00:56:33.589
And the problem
is that with his
astral body gone.

683
00:56:33.656 --> 00:56:37.893
he's just left us
with a physical body.
an empty vessel.

684
00:56:37.960 --> 00:56:41.564
And there are
entities that know this
because they can smell it.

685
00:56:41.631 --> 00:56:44.300
That's why they're
gathered around him.

686
00:56:44.367 --> 00:56:46.603
Are these the things
that I've been seeing?

687
00:56:53.509 --> 00:56:55.845
They're all trying
to get inside
of his physical body

688
00:56:55.912 --> 00:56:57.646
simply because they...

689
00:56:57.713 --> 00:56:59.582
They crave life.

690
00:56:59.648 --> 00:57:01.584
the chance
to live again.

691
00:57:01.651 --> 00:57:04.453
But there are
other entities

692
00:57:04.520 --> 00:57:06.356
who are malevolent

693
00:57:07.790 --> 00:57:10.260
and have a more
insidious agenda.

694
00:57:11.494 --> 00:57:13.763
And then.
there's this.

695
00:57:16.031 --> 00:57:20.570
A demon who
seeks Dalton's body
for one reason.

696
00:57:21.737 --> 00:57:23.873
to cause
pain to others.

697
00:57:27.076 --> 00:57:28.744
He is so desperate
to possess Dalton.

698
00:57:28.811 --> 00:57:31.714
and he's the closest
of all the entities to
getting inside of him.

699
00:57:31.781 --> 00:57:33.682
What do you mean
the closest?

700
00:57:33.749 --> 00:57:37.186
Because these entities.
they can't just walk into
the bodies of the living

701
00:57:37.253 --> 00:57:38.587
anytime they please.

702
00:57:38.654 --> 00:57:40.456
To cross over
from their realm.

703
00:57:40.523 --> 00:57:42.458
it takes time.
It takes energy.

704
00:57:42.525 --> 00:57:45.962
But the longer that
Dalton's astral body

705
00:57:46.029 --> 00:57:50.433
is kept away
from his physical body.
the weaker the link gets.

706
00:57:52.068 --> 00:57:54.670
The easier it is
to possess him.

707
00:57:54.737 --> 00:57:58.241
Is there
anything we can do
to bring Dalton back?

708
00:58:03.345 --> 00:58:04.614
There's something
we could try.

709
00:58:05.781 --> 00:58:08.084
It's a little unorthodox.

710
00:58:09.719 --> 00:58:12.521
But I would need
your complete trust.

711
00:58:12.588 --> 00:58:15.090
No. no. no. I'm sorry.
this has gone too far.

712
00:58:15.157 --> 00:58:17.160
What? No. please. Josh.
You said you would
give her a chance.

713
00:58:17.226 --> 00:58:18.927
I have given her
a chance. honey.

714
00:58:18.994 --> 00:58:20.829
but I can't have
somebody coming
into our home

715
00:58:20.896 --> 00:58:22.197
and telling us
that the reason
our son is in a coma

716
00:58:22.264 --> 00:58:24.501
is because his soul
has floated off

717
00:58:24.567 --> 00:58:25.668
somewhere
in another dimension.

718
00:58:25.735 --> 00:58:27.303
We're gonna bring her
all the way here

719
00:58:27.369 --> 00:58:29.505
and not even consider
what she's saying?

720
00:58:29.572 --> 00:58:34.544
I did this to make sure
you could feel at ease.
And if it helped. great.

721
00:58:34.610 --> 00:58:38.815
I've listened to
the dog and pony show.
I have seen the drawings.

722
00:58:38.881 --> 00:58:40.549
But to bring
Dalton into it. no.

723
00:58:40.616 --> 00:58:42.285
But why is our son
still in a coma?

724
00:58:42.351 --> 00:58:44.586
Why can't
the doctors tell us
what is wrong with him?

725
00:58:44.653 --> 00:58:47.623
How did the voice
of reason become
the bad guy here?

726
00:58:47.690 --> 00:58:50.226
Don't you see. Renai?
You want to believe.
Anybody would.

727
00:58:50.293 --> 00:58:53.263
You don't believe me!
You don't believe me!

728
00:58:57.199 --> 00:58:59.602
I moved houses for you.

729
00:58:59.668 --> 00:59:03.673
What do you mean.
I don't believe you?
I'm on your side here.

730
00:59:05.674 --> 00:59:10.746
But this.
this is dangerous
and exploitative.

731
00:59:10.813 --> 00:59:13.549
You guys come
into the home of
a seriously ill child.

732
00:59:13.616 --> 00:59:17.586
and you make some
tenuous connection
between him

733
00:59:17.653 --> 00:59:21.757
and the images my wife
is seeing. and voila!

734
00:59:21.824 --> 00:59:25.495
Tears validate your power.
and thank you very much.
that will be $600 please.

735
00:59:25.561 --> 00:59:25.561
Thank you for coming.

736
00:59:25.561 --> 00:59:26.996
Please. Please.

737
00:59:27.062 --> 00:59:27.062
Thank you.
No. I really understand.

738
00:59:27.062 --> 00:59:29.866
Please.

739
00:59:29.932 --> 00:59:32.669
Thank you for
your hospitality.
Good luck.

740
00:59:33.168 --> 00:59:35.371
Oh. Jesus!

741
00:59:35.438 --> 00:59:37.106
Sorry to waste your time.

742
00:59:41.377 --> 00:59:42.745
JOSH: Where are you. buddy?

743
00:59:46.081 --> 00:59:48.184
Did you go somewhere?

744
00:59:49.919 --> 00:59:51.154
No.

745
00:59:52.689 --> 00:59:57.226
No. you're right here.
You are right here.

746
01:00:00.363 --> 01:00:02.031
Can you hear me?

747
01:00:04.900 --> 01:00:08.471
I know you can hear me.
but you gotta show me.
okay. buddy?

748
01:00:08.538 --> 01:00:11.507
You gotta show me
that you can hear me.

749
01:01:11.033 --> 01:01:12.535
(SOBBING)

750
01:01:25.548 --> 01:01:26.683
Okay.

751
01:01:39.862 --> 01:01:41.563
What's most important
is that you realize

752
01:01:41.630 --> 01:01:43.299
no two attempts
are the same.

753
01:01:43.366 --> 01:01:46.235
I'm going to be
completely honest
with you about the results.

754
01:01:46.302 --> 01:01:49.205
If there's no
dialogue established.
I'm gonna tell you.

755
01:01:51.674 --> 01:01:53.442
 TUCKER: <i> These</i>
 <i> still cameras are rigged</i>

756
01:01:53.509 --> 01:01:55.511
 <i> to pick up any changes</i>
 <i> in the atmosphere.</i>

757
01:01:55.577 --> 01:01:59.115
 <i> both electrical</i>
 <i> or temperature-wise.</i>

758
01:02:00.316 --> 01:02:03.385
 <i> Don't be alarmed</i>
 <i> if they go off.</i>

759
01:02:03.452 --> 01:02:06.989
ELISE: <i> You're gonna see
 a lot of confusing things.
 things you don't understand.</i>

760
01:02:07.055 --> 01:02:11.193
But do not question them
and do not speak in any way.

761
01:02:11.260 --> 01:02:13.328
I want you to know
whatever I say
when I'm in tune

762
01:02:13.395 --> 01:02:16.031
is going to be
at a very low volume.
You won't hear any of it.

763
